    "body": "Formal stable release v1.0.81 \u2014 2026-10-23\n\nDocker commit: 7f2898026b114d2ada3ecf8278af46eebd5c9948\nEngine: 6d8d759428cf8049f5b8f4c4894022b897fd3229\nPlugins: 81b3f71febc79491c1cb0b59487bb551b255c14d\nAdapters: 9f7732138c72723f10a5a5aafaaa3d1a4e6282d1\n\nImage: ghcr.io/jfroebe/metadata-engine-docker@sha256:c91d8d9e1fc3b3c1eb97f026381ad52ba2fee14108cbb8060d0e39d131db950a\nTags: 1.0.81, stable, latest\nTested platform: linux/amd64\n\nIncludes movie, TV, book and audiobook metadata; Performer Explorer and photography; music foundation; content warnings; Plex integration.\n\nValidation: exact pinned source suites, cross-repository contracts, packaged HTTP and music/cache tests, JavaScript syntax, native Plex prepublication gate, independent registry tag pulls, component provenance, pulled-image runtime and health.\nWorkflow evidence: https://github.com/jfroebe/metadata-engine-docker/actions/runs/39946223207\n\nLimitations: only the platform listed above is validated. Source APIs retain their credential, availability and terms requirements. See PR #59 for premerge checks, skips and warnings.\n\nUpgrade: back up configuration and databases, record the current image digest, then separately authorize deployment using the immutable image above. No production deployment was performed.\nRollback: stop the upgraded container, restore the recorded prior image digest and matching configuration/database backup, then restart. Do not use mutable tags as rollback identifiers."
  },
